--TEST--
an `extend` block on a `Core` class may add an enum but not an attribute: no class can extend a `Core` class, so an attribute declared on it could be used nowhere, and the error names the file-scope declaration to write instead — `rule:classes/an-extend-block-adds-members-to-a-type`
--FILE--
<?nvs
namespace Shop;

use Core\Time\Date;
use Shop\Calendar;

extend Date as Calendar {
    enum Season { Winter, Summer }

    attribute Holiday on method { name: string }
}

echo Date::Season::Summer == Date::Season::Winter ? "same" : "different", "\n";
// covers: lang:classes/extend-blocks
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0338]: an `extend` block cannot add an attribute to `Core\Time\Date`, because no class can extend or implement it
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
